{"id": "tea:siddhantalesasangraha:1", "source": "src:siddhantalesasangraha", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Collects the views on Īśvara and jīva: the Vivaraṇa (Īśvara the prototype, jīva the reflection in ignorance), the Saṃkṣepaśārīraka (Īśvara reflected in ignorance, jīva in the intellect), the semblance view of the Vārttika, the limitation view of Vācaspati, and the one-jīva view; and on whether hearing is enjoined and which of hearing and contemplation is principal.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:how-the-one-appears-as-many", "cpt:avaccheda-vada", "cpt:pratibimba-vada", "cpt:abhasa-vada"], "disputes": ["dsp:how-the-one-appears-as-many", "dsp:sravana-alone-liberates"], "teachers": ["tch:appayya-diksita"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
